Protocol Buffers (protobuf) - built from source at build time from public upstream.

Component:   protobuf (libprotobuf, protoc)
Upstream:    https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf
Version:     pinned by PROTOBUF_TAG in tools/unitrace/cmake/Perfetto.cmake, the
             single source of truth (not repeated here)
License:     BSD-3-Clause (see ./LICENSE)

How it is used: scripts/get_protobuf.py clones PROTOBUF_TAG (shallow) and builds
protobuf as static, position-independent libraries into
<build>/protobuf-install. libprotobuf is linked statically into unitrace_tool
with hidden symbols; protoc is a build-time tool only and is not shipped. Never
taken from a system install.

To bump: update PROTOBUF_TAG in tools/unitrace/cmake/Perfetto.cmake, refresh
LICENSE from upstream at the new tag, and update
tools/unitrace/third-party-programs.txt if the license changed.
